  "file_attributes": [
    {
      "doc_text": " Implementations for `uN::extract_bits` and `uN::deposit_bits`",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        0,
        65
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": "",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        66,
        69
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " For the purposes of this implementation, the operations can be thought",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        70,
        144
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " of as operating on the input bits as a list, starting from the least",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        145,
        217
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " significant bit. Extraction is like `Vec::retain` that deletes bits",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        218,
        289
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " where the mask has a zero. Deposition is like doing the inverse by",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        290,
        360
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " inserting the zeros that extraction would delete.",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        361,
        414
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": "",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        415,
        418
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " Key observation: Each extracted or deposited bit needs to be",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        419,
        483
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " shifted by the count of zeros up to the corresponding mask bit.",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        484,
        551
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": "",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        552,
        555
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " With that in mind, the general idea is to decompose the operation into",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        556,
        630
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " a sequence of stages in `0..log2(BITS)`, where each stage shifts some",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        631,
        704
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " of the bits by `n = 1 << stage`. The masks for each stage are computed",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        705,
        779
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " via prefix counts of zeros in the mask.",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        780,
        823
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": "",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        824,
        827
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " # Extraction",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        828,
        844
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": "",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        845,
        848
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " Consider the input as a sequence of runs of data (bitstrings A,B,C,...),",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        849,
        925
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " split by fixed-width groups of zeros ('.'), initially at width `n = 1`.",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        926,
        1001
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " Counting the groups of zeros, each stage shifts the odd-indexed runs of",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        1002,
        1077
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " data right by `n`, effectively swapping them with the preceding zeros.",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        1078,
        1152
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " For the next stage, `n` is doubled as all the zeros are now paired.",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        1153,
        1224
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " ```text",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        1225,
        1236
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " .A.B.C.D.E.F.G.H",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        1237,
        1257
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " ..AB..CD..EF..GH",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        1258,
        1278
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " ....ABCD....EFGH",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        1279,
        1299
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " ........ABCDEFGH",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        1300,
        1320
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " ```",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        1321,
        1328
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " What makes this nontrivial is that the lengths of the bitstrings are not",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        1329,
        1405
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " the same. Using lowercase for individual bits, the above might look like",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        1406,
        1482
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " ```text",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        1483,
        1494
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " .a.bbb.ccccc.dd.e..g.hh",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        1495,
        1522
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " ..abbb..cccccdd..e..ghh",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        1523,
        1550
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " ....abbbcccccdd....eghh",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        1551,
        1578
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " ........abbbcccccddeghh",
      "path": "doc",
      "range": [
        1579,
        1606
      ],
      "style": "inner"
    },
    {
      "doc_text": " ```",
      "path": "doc",
